SPERR -- vendored into SZ3
==========================

Upstream:  https://github.com/NCAR/SPERR, release v0.8.4
License:   Apache License 2.0 (see the LICENSE file in this directory)

The files in this directory are derived from, and modified from, the upstream
SPERR sources listed above. This notice is provided under section 4(b) of the
Apache License 2.0. The modifications made by the SZ3 project are:

1. Namespace change. Every occurrence of `namespace sperr` was re-wrapped as
   `namespace SZ3::SPERR`, so that SZ3 can be linked alongside an independent
   build of upstream SPERR without symbol collisions.

2. Header-only amalgamation. Upstream ships an implementation in separate
   translation units; SZ3 is a header-only library. The following 13 upstream
   .cpp files were inlined into the single header `sperr_core_impl.hpp`, with
   their contents marked by `// ---- BEGIN <file> ----` /
   `// ---- END <file> ----` provenance comments:

       sperr_helper.cpp    Bitstream.cpp        Bitmask.cpp
       Conditioner.cpp     CDF97.cpp            SPECK_INT.cpp
       SPECK3D_INT.cpp     SPECK3D_INT_ENC.cpp  SPECK3D_INT_DEC.cpp
       SPECK1D_INT.cpp     SPECK1D_INT_ENC.cpp  SPECK1D_INT_DEC.cpp
       Outlier_Coder.cpp

3. Subsetting. Only the compression core is vendored (CDF97 wavelet transform,
   SPECK 1D/2D/3D integer and float coders, Conditioner, Outlier_Coder,
   Bitmask/Bitstream, SPERR3D OMP drivers, stream tools). Upstream's CLI tools,
   build system, and test suite are not included.

4. Macro guard. `SPERRHeaderOnly.hpp` saves, undefines, and restores the `PSNR`
   macro around its includes, to avoid a collision with the global `PSNR` macro
   defined by SZ3's C API wrapper (tools/sz3c).

The following files in this directory were written by the SZ3 project and are
not upstream SPERR code: `SperrConfig.h`, `SPERRHeaderOnly.hpp`,
`SPERRTypes.hpp`.

Upstream files are otherwise unmodified and carry no per-file copyright notices
of their own; upstream's own attribution comments have been retained verbatim,
including the QccPack acknowledgement at the top of `CDF97.h`.

Citation: S. Li, P. Lindstrom, J. Clyne, "Lossy Scientific Data Compression
With SPERR," IPDPS 2023, pp. 1007-1017. doi:10.1109/IPDPS54959.2023.00104
